============================================================
PART 7 — HOW SANCTUM LOGIN WORKS
============================================================

STEP 8: API LOGIN
------------------------------------------------------------

Request:

POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/login


JSON body:

{
    "email": "john@gmail.com",
    "password": "password"
}


Laravel executes:

Auth::attempt($credentials)


If successful:

$user = Auth::user();


Then:

$token = $user->createToken('api-token')->plainTextToken;


Response:

{
    "message": "Login successful",
    "user": {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "John",
        "email": "john@gmail.com"
    },
    "token": "1|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
}


IMPORTANT:

The token is used by the API client for future requests.


============================================================
PART 8 — SANCTUM PROTECTED ROUTE
============================================================

STEP 9: Protect an API route
------------------------------------------------------------

This:

Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')->group(function () {

});


means:

Only authenticated Sanctum users can access these routes.


Example:

Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')->get('/user', function (Request $request) {

    return $request->user();

});


The request must contain:

Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN


Example:

Authorization: Bearer 1|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


Without a valid token:

401 Unauthorized


With a valid token:

The authenticated user is returned.


